From: elden <elden@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] monitor: assume output is on when output power mode setup fails

phosh requests a zwlr_output_power_v1 object per monitor in
phosh_monitor_constructed(). That request can fail: wlroots only allows a
single zwlr_output_power_v1 object per wlr_output, so whenever another
client (wlopm, a debug tool, a second shell instance during session
handover) already owns the object for the primary panel, the wpd request
is answered with the "failed" event and phosh never sees mode changes.

wlr_output_power_handle_failed() only emits a warning. PhoshMonitor keeps
the initial power_mode value, which is PHOSH_MONITOR_POWER_SAVE_MODE_OFF,
and PhoshScreenSaverManager derives its "active" state from it
(screen-saver-manager.c: on_primary_monitor_power_mode_changed()):

    active = (mode == PHOSH_MONITOR_POWER_SAVE_MODE_OFF);

So the shell starts up believing the panel is already off. "active" is
TRUE from the first frame and never changes again, because no further
power-mode notifications can arrive. The user visible consequences are:

 * org.gnome.ScreenSaver.GetActive() returns TRUE while the panel is lit,
   and GetActiveTime() stays at 0;
 * a short press on the power key does nothing, because
   on_power_button_pressed() returns early for both the press and the
   release half while self->active is TRUE (screen-saver-manager.c:218);
 * idle blanking never happens either, for the same reason.

Suspending from the power menu keeps working, as that path goes through
logind and does not consult "active", which makes the failure mode
confusing to diagnose.

Treating the power mode as ON when the request fails is the semantically
correct default: we could not establish any knowledge about the panel, and
a lit panel is the only state consistent with the shell being able to draw.
Signed-off-by: <author>
---
 src/monitor/monitor.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/monitor/monitor.c b/src/monitor/monitor.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/monitor/monitor.c
+++ b/src/monitor/monitor.c
@@ -266,9 +266,19 @@ wlr_output_power_handle_failed(void *data,
 {
   PhoshMonitor *self = PHOSH_MONITOR (data);
+  GObject *object = G_OBJECT (self);
 
   g_return_if_fail (PHOSH_IS_MONITOR (self));
   g_warning("Failed to set output power mode for %s\n", self->name);
+
+  /* Without a working zwlr_output_power_v1 we can never learn about power
+   * mode changes, so react as if the output was still on. Otherwise the
+   * screensaver manager starts out considering the screen blanked and the
+   * power button becomes a no-op. */
+  if (self->power_mode != PHOSH_MONITOR_POWER_SAVE_MODE_ON) {
+    self->power_mode = PHOSH_MONITOR_POWER_SAVE_MODE_ON;
+    g_object_notify (object, "power-mode");
+  }
 }
